From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:51:47 -0400
Subject: feat: the address field's width as a setting, and no Ask Google line

GitHub issue 14 (toolbar T48, privacy Q17). Settings > Stedding > Address
field offers Full width, the default (T29), or a field centred on the page
at 800, 640 or 480 DIP. A centred field keeps its width and place in every
state, the suggestions open under it at its width, and the empty row either
side of it moves the window: the two spacers are views of their own class
that the caption hit test passes through. The spacers now always exist and
are shown with a centred width; a change applies at once. A positive
`location_bar_width` still overrides the setting.

The focused field no longer offers "Ask Google about this page" with
Google as the engine: Chromium's OmniboxContextualSearchOnFocusSuggestions
is off, as the rest of that family already was.

Why: the owner asked for both on 2026-10-28.
Removable when: never as a feature; the toolbar hunks go if Chromium's
toolbar grows its own width setting.
